.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt UUSTAT 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uustat
.Nd list, summarize and cancel queued uucp jobs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl s Ar system
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl k Ar job
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads the queue under
.Pa /var/spool/uucp
and prints, summarizes or cancels jobs.
Without
.Fl a
or
.Fl u ,
only jobs for the current user are shown.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Include every user.
.It Fl q
Print a one-line summary of job, system and user counts.
.It Fl s Ar system
Select one destination system.
.It Fl u Ar user
Select one requesting user.
.It Fl k Ar job
Cancel the numbered job.
.El
.Pp
A list line is
.D1 Ar id user system grade kind state
where
.Ar state
is
.Ql queued .
The queue format and peer configuration are documented in
.Xr uucp 1
and
.Pa docs/posix/P4-uucp.md .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/spool/uucp -compact
.It Pa /etc/uucp/config
Peer and spool configuration.
.It Pa /var/spool/uucp/queue
Queued job records.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A missing job or queue error exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uucp 1 ,
.Xr uux 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the documented list, summary and cancel subset. The
.Fl e ,
.Fl i ,
.Fl o ,
.Fl r ,
.Fl W ,
.Fl y
and
.Fl z
forms are not implemented.
